content.text:
Saving now commits a typed-but-unadded custom model ID instead of silently dropping it.

The change extracts the add-model logic into a single `addCustomModel` function on the component that reads and writes the form store directly (`form.getFieldValue` / `form.setFieldValue`), so it can be called from three places: the `+` button, the Enter key, and the form's submit handler right before `form.handleSubmit()`. Because the store update is synchronous, the submit reads the already-updated `enabledModels`.

```135:147:apps/frontend/src/components/settings/llm-provider-form.tsx
	const isCustomModel = (modelId: string) => !currentModels.some((m) => m.id === modelId);

